          "title": "Black Monday",
          "subtitle": "Accumulation",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Black Monday is a 1988 commercial card game where cards represent shares of stock that rise or fall during play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Published by Hexagames in 1988, Black Monday turns stock-market movement into a card-driven economic game of changing share values."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2-6 players use the table arrangement described for Black Monday."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Dedicated Black Monday stock-market card deck"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Dedicated Black Monday stock-market card deck, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal stock and market cards from the dedicated deck and prepare the share-value or market area for play."
            }
